# Component Library Conventions

When creating or modifying UI in `apps/web`, follow these conventions for visual consistency and maintainability.

## Use Primitives First

- **Buttons** → Use `Button` from `@/components/ui/button` (not raw `<button>`)
- **Inputs** → Use `Input` from `@/components/ui/input` (not raw `<input>`)
- **Cards** → Use `Card`, `CardHeader`, `CardContent`, etc. from `@/components/ui/card` (not custom divs with shadow/border)
- **Navigation** → Use `Link` from `next/link` for any clickable element that navigates to an internal route (not `router.push` + `onClick`). This yields crawlable `<a>` tags, prefetch-on-hover, and instant `loading.tsx` skeletons. Reserve `router.push` for programmatic navigation (e.g. form submissions, redirects after async actions).

Add new primitives via `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <component>` when needed.

## Semantic Colors

Use theme tokens instead of raw Tailwind colors:

| Prefer | Avoid |
|--------|-------|
| `bg-primary`, `text-primary-foreground` | `bg-stone-800`, `text-white` |
| `text-muted-foreground` | `text-stone-500` |
| `bg-muted`, `bg-card` | `bg-stone-200`, `bg-white` |
| `border-border` | `border-stone-200` |

## Small, Focused Components

- Keep components doing one thing; compose larger UIs from smaller pieces
- Extract repeated patterns into reusable components
- Prefer props over inline logic when it improves clarity

## Storybook Stories

- Add `*.stories.tsx` for new components (CSF3 format)
- Document key states: default, disabled, loading, empty, error
- Use `Components/` or `Components/UI/` in the story title

## Before Adding New UI

1. Check if a primitive exists in `src/components/ui/`
2. Check if a composed component already solves the need
3. Add a Storybook story when introducing a new component
4. Fatal `try/catch` (no rethrow): call `Sentry.captureException` when DSN is set — [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](../../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#error-monitoring-sentry)
